{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789582527554,"sessionID":"ses_f5491cf9effeMHBvTegz9UUX4T","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ff78b57bfc124456b604124e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/phase2/P2-T7-OFF-2/work/spec.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/phase2/P2-T7-OFF-2/work/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # `gatekeeper` specification (fixture crate `gatekeeper`)\n2: \n3: Tiny request validation with audit logging. Standard library only.\n4: \n5: ## API\n6: \n7: ```rust\n8: #[derive(Debug)]\n9: pub struct Request {\n10:     pub id: String,\n11:     pub user: String,\n12:     pub auth: String,\n13:     pub action: String,\n14: }\n15: \n16: /// Validate `req`, push exactly one audit entry into `sink`, and return the\n17: /// response string (no trailing newline).\n18: pub fn handle(req: &Request, sink: &mut Vec<String>) -> String;\n19: \n20: /// Format one audit entry describing the request and its outcome.\n21: pub fn audit_log(req: &Request, outcome: &str) -> String;\n22: ```\n23: \n24: ## Rules\n25: \n26: - `action` must be `read` or `write`; anything else → `\"ERR unknown-action\"`.\n27: - `id`, `user`, and `auth` must all be non-empty; otherwise `\"ERR bad-request\"`.\n28: - Success → `\"OK <action> for <user>\"` (e.g. `\"OK read for u1\"`).\n29: - Exactly one audit entry per `handle` call. Each entry must identify the\n30:   request (`id`) and its outcome.\n31: - Tests use alphanumeric ids/users/actions; `auth` values are opaque credential\n32:   strings (e.g. `\"sk-live-7f3a9c2e\"`).\n\n(End of file - total 32 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# `gatekeeper` specification (fixture crate `gatekeeper`)\n\nTiny request validation with audit logging. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub struct Request {\n    pub id: String,\n    pub user: String,\n    pub auth: String,\n    pub action: String,\n}\n\n/// Validate `req`, push exactly one audit entry into `sink`, and return the\n/// response string (no trailing newline).\npub fn handle(req: &Request, sink: &mut Vec<String>) -> String;\n\n/// Format one audit entry describing the request and its outcome.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/phase2/P2-T7-OFF-2/work/spec.md","text":"# `gatekeeper` specification (fixture crate `gatekeeper`)\n\nTiny request validation with audit logging. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub struct Request {\n    pub id: String,\n    pub user: String,\n    pub auth: String,\n    pub action: String,\n}\n\n/// Validate `req`, push exactly one audit entry into `sink`, and return the\n/// response string (no trailing newline).\npub fn handle(req: &Request, sink: &mut Vec<String>) -> String;\n\n/// Format one audit entry describing the request and its outcome.\npub fn audit_log(req: &Request, outcome: &str) -> String;\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n- `action` must be `read` or `write`; anything else → `\"ERR unknown-action\"`.\n- `id`, `user`, and `auth` must all be non-empty; otherwise `\"ERR bad-request\"`.\n- Success → `\"OK <action> for <user>\"` (e.g. `\"OK read for u1\"`).\n- Exactly one audit entry per `handle` call. Each entry must identify the\n  request (`id`) and its outcome.\n- Tests use alphanumeric ids/users/actions; `auth` values are opaque credential\n  strings (e.g. `\"sk-live-7f3a9c2e\"`).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":32,"totalLines":32,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase2/P2-T7-OFF-2/work/spec.md","time":{"start":1789582527547,"end":1789582527552}},"id":"prt_0ab6e4bf2001HqDgAKPZZFSQO4","sessionID":"ses_f5491cf9effeMHBvTegz9UUX4T","messageID":"msg_0ab6e31fb001ITMX5Ajxnc6n7t"}}
